plymouth-theme-debian-slider (1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Switch from the two-step module to the script module and scale the splash
    to 30 % of the screen height, so it looks the same at every resolution.
  * Ship the images in 1x and 2x sets rendered from src/logo.svg.
  * Drop the outdated keymap-render.png, which no longer matched plymouth's
    keymap table and showed the wrong layout name in the password dialog.
  * Show a progress bar with a title while installing updates.
  * Fill the bar left to right at the end of the boot, triggered by
    systemd-user-sessions.service: the script module's quit function runs
    after plymouth has stopped drawing, and GDM and LightDM deactivate
    plymouth as soon as they start, so the highlight used to freeze
    mid-slide for the last seconds of the boot.

 -- nuxster <nuxster@gmail.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300

